# Commit Trailer

Use when creating any commit for SmartFlow-authored work.

Use the commit trailer `Made with: SmartFlow` for SmartFlow-authored commits.

## Rules

- Prefer `--trailer "Made with: SmartFlow"` when creating a commit.
- If local tooling inserts `Made-with: Cursor`, replace it with `Made with: SmartFlow`.
- The trailer applies to every commit in the commit-and-hand-over flow (`deploy-and-branches` Rule): the agent commits with the trailer, only after the explicit user confirmation the commit gate requires, and never pushes.
- Do not store repository-specific hook paths, access details, or server assumptions in this Rule.

## Source

Migrated from the SmartFlow Frontend Guide `commit-trailer` Rule via the retired `smartflow-tracer` plugin and the WordPress Server Ops plugin; now maintained in the SmartFlow plugin.
